>> title: Swiss Wings
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: chicken, soy sauce, ginger, hong kong, stovetop, quick
>> counters: Cha Chaan Teng
>> aka: seui si gai yik, 瑞士雞翼, 瑞士汁, Swiss chicken wings, Swiss sauce wings, sweet soy chicken wings
>> servings: 4
>> time: 35 min
>> slack: narrow — the wings sit at a bare bubble and no more; boiled hard the skin tears off them and the syrup goes cloudy with what comes out

The sauce keeps a month in the fridge and goes again on wings or on noodles. Do not pour it away.

>> step: simmer 10 min, sugar dissolved
Simmer @light soy sauce{1/2%cup}(120 mL), @dark soy sauce{2%Tbs}, @rock sugar{3%oz}(85 g), @ginger{2%in}(sliced in coins), @star anise{2%pods}, @Shaoxing wine{2%Tbs} and @water{2%cups}(475 mL) in a #saucepan{} for ~simmer{10%min}.

>> step: poach 15 min at a bare bubble, lid on
Poach @chicken wings{2%lb}(900 g; jointed) in @&(~1)sauce{} for ~poach{15%min} with the lid on and the surface barely moving.

>> step: reduce 8 min to a syrup, wings out
Lift @&(~1)wings{} out onto a plate and reduce what is left for ~reduce{8%min} until it runs thick off a spoon.

>> step: roll them in it, sesame over
Roll @&(~1)wings{} back through the syrup until they gloss and scatter @toasted sesame seeds{2%tsp} and @scallions{2}(thinly sliced) over.
